        "supplementalExactTextAssertions": 22,
        "supplementalPlacementAssertions": 22,
        "relation": "The ten vertically aligned pairs are (1,1), (2,4), (3,9), (4,16), (5,25), (6,36), (7,49), (8,64), (9,81), (10,100). Each lower entry equals the square of its own upper index.",
        "relationEvidenceLimit": "The native spec does not assert a square-function formula; exact source values, cell placement, and independent visual comparison establish the pairing. No plotted point relationships exist, so pointRelationships/displacement assertions are not applicable."
      },
      "observations": [
        "Compared the original and recovery4 preview once each. Both have one two-row, eleven-column table including the two headers, twenty numeric labels, and no omitted subfigure or extra cell.",
        "The upper row reads n followed by 1 through 10; the lower row reads a with subscript n followed by 1, 4, 9, 16, 25, 36, 49, 64, 81, 100. Every value is under the correct index. In particular the final 10/100 column is present, readable, and not clipped.",
        "The recovery4 pixels visibly show the actual lowered n glyph attached to a, not an underscore, baseline an, empty glyph, or replacement box. SVG/browser records encode the label as a\\u2099. The label's reported positive browser box is 19.21875 by 22 px; its 20 px text setting is the containing label font size, not a claim that the smaller subscript glyph is 20 px tall.",
        "The source-lattice inventory requires and maps to full-table-2-by-11, a native gridDimensions assertion on table-lattice. The 616 by 128 px lattice with 56 by 64 px cells independently yields 11 columns and 2 rows; objectCount alone is not being used to prove the grid.",
        "At its actual 640 px scroll-media width, the 640 by 320 browser preview has dark ink, muted gray rules, and white paper. All 22 labels are clearly visible with positive recorded browser boxes, 20 px nominal text, clear cell margins, and no collision or clipped border. The longest value 100 has a 33.375 px-wide box inside its 56 px cell.",
        "The source's wider first column and open outer sides are not preserved literally. The spec explicitly identifies equal-width columns and closed side borders as modern additions. They preserve every cell and relation while removing scan texture and improving regularity.",
        "The approved lesson introduces these exact ten terms as an already-given finite sequence and places this table after its explanation of tabular representation. This is instructional given data, not a solved exercise. Exercises 204 through 217 have no figure reference to this table; no new formula, worked answer, solution annotation, or answer-key content appears in the preview.",
        "Visible labels are only Latin mathematical n and a with subscript n plus the original numbers. No Cyrillic or Chinese wording, cultural symbol, flag, portrait, archival texture, unit typo, sign change, or decorative source artifact leaked into the modern figure.",
        "The current spec's source.image names the durable original under ssot-resources, with the independently checked original SHA. The current SVG and render hashes match the recovery4 record's preserved unmodified files; the existing native validator/render PASS and supplemental cell-check PASS are reused as mechanical evidence, not producer approval.",
        "This pass is for the exact current figure and observed browser preview. Scratch render output paths still require the parent's portable promotion and metadata rebinding. Final offline lesson integration, reachable mobile horizontal scroll end, and alternate theme/print rendering were not re-tested in this constrained reviewer."
      ]
